ximize early opportunities in the workplace and obtain competitive placements upon graduation\nVisit The Center for Spartan Engineering\nAlumni\nToggle submenu\nAlumni Board\nAlumni Awards\nGet Involved\nUpdate Your Information\nMany options for giving to the college are available\nGive Now\nGive\nToggle submenu\nWays to Give\nFunding Priorities\nAnnual Giving\nAll University Campaign\nCreate an Endowment\nDonor Recognition\nDecoding Generosity\nEndowed Professorships\nNews and Events\nToggle submenu\nNews\nEvents\nSpartan Engineering E-News\nMedia and Public Relations\nVolunteering\nSign up to receive the quarterly Spartan Engineering E-News packed with updates within the college\nSubscribe to E-News\nFaculty/Staff Intranet\nGraduate Studies\nBreadcrumb\nHome\nAcademics\nWelcome to Graduate Studies\nAt the College of Engineering at Michigan State University, our graduate students collaborate with faculty and researchers across campus and the world to take on challenges in areas such as sustainability, security, materials, health, and energy.\nCurrent Graduate Students\nFuture Graduate Students\nAcademic Departments\nResearch Priorities\nDegree Programs\nAcademic Departments\nFaculty and staff in eight academic departments prepare talented Spartans to compete with the best in the world and build a better tomorrow.\nBiomedical Engineering\nBiosystems and Agricultural Engineering\nChemical Engineering and Materials Science\nCivil and Environmental Engineering\nComputational Mathematics, Science and Engineering\nComputer Science and Engineering\nElectrical and Computer Engineering\nMechanical Engineering\nResearch Priorities\nThe College of Engineering focuses on seven priority areas for research and innovation that drive economic development and cover a broad range of domains.\nApplied Electromagnetics\nComputational and Informational Systems\nHealth and Biomedical\nMaterials, Mechanics, and Advanced Manufacturing\nMobility and Robotics\nSmartAg\nSustainability: Infrastructure, Environment, Energy, and Water\nResearch Priorities\nDegree Programs\nThe MSU College of Engineering offers M.S. and Ph.D. degree programs across eleven engineering and computer science disciplines, giving our graduate students the opportunity to find their niche and pursue their dreams.\nMaster of Science (M.S.)\nBiomedical Engineering (M.S.)\nBiosystems Engineering (M.S.)\nChemical Engineering (M.S.)\nCivil Engineering \u2013 Online (M.S.)\nCivil Engineering (M.S.)\nComputational Mathematics, Science and Engineering (M.S.)\nComputer Science (M.S.)\nElectrical and Computer Engineering \u2013 Online (M.S.)\nElectrical and Computer Engineering (M.S.)\nEngineering Mechanics (M.S.)\nEnvironmental Engineering (M.S.)\nMaterials Science and Engineering (M.S.)\nMechanical Engineering - Online (M.S.)\nMechanical Engineering (M.S.)\nDoctor of Philosophy (Ph.D.)\nBiomedical Engineering (Ph.D.)\nBiosystems Engineering (Ph.D.)\nChemical Engineering (Ph.D.)\nCivil Engineering (Ph.D.)\nComputational Mathematics, Science and Engineering (Ph.D.)\nComputer Science (Ph.D.)\nElectrical and Computer Engineering (Ph.D.)\nEngineering Mechanics (Ph.D.)\nEnvironmental Engineering (Ph.D.)\nMaterials Science and Engineering (Ph.D.)\nMechanical Engineering (Ph.D.)\nDual Ph.D. Programs\nCertificates\nComputational Modeling\nData-enabled Water Sustainability and Equity\nHigh Performance Computing\nFoundations in Chemical Engineering\nFoundations in Material Science and Engineering\nSecure and Connected Cyber-Physical Systems\nSemiconductor Manufacturing, Processing, and Devices\nGraduate Studies\nMaster's Program\nPh.D. Programs\nDual Ph.D. Programs\nOnline Programs\nGraduate Handbooks\nGraduate Certificates\nContact Us\nGraduate Admissions\nAcademic Departments\nApplied Engineering Sciences\nBiomedical Engineering\nBiosystems and Agricultural Engineering\nChemical Engineering and Materials Science\nCivil and Environmental Engineering\nComputational Mathematics, Science and Engineeri